+# Deploying Fizzy on one server
+
+The root Kamal configuration deploys the OSS edition as a single web container on
+one Linux server. It uses the app's SQLite databases, local Active Storage, and
+Solid Queue worker embedded in Puma. The named Docker volume mounted at
+`/rails/storage` keeps SQLite databases, queued jobs, and uploaded files across
+container replacements and deploys.
+
+## Requirements
+
+- A Linux server with Docker installed and reachable over SSH as a user Kamal can
+  use (with permission to run Docker).
+- A DNS `A` record for your hostname pointing to the server. Ports 80 and 443
+  must be reachable from the internet; Kamal Proxy obtains and renews the TLS
+  certificate.
+- A Docker Hub account/repository where Kamal can push the built image.
+- An SMTP server that can send email from your chosen From address.
+- Ruby and the project dependencies installed locally, and Kamal available via
+  `bin/kamal`.
+
+## Configure
+
+Set these variables in the shell you use for Kamal (or export them from a
+private, untracked environment file):
+
+```sh
+export FIZZY_HOST=fizzy.example.com
+export FIZZY_SERVER_IP=203.0.113.10
+export KAMAL_REGISTRY_USERNAME=your-docker-hub-username
+export KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD=your-docker-hub-access-token
+export RAILS_MASTER_KEY="$(openssl rand -hex 16)"
+export SECRET_KEY_BASE="$(bin/rails secret)"
+export SMTP_ADDRESS=smtp.example.com
+export SMTP_PORT=587
+export SMTP_DOMAIN=fizzy.example.com
+export SMTP_USERNAME=your-smtp-username
+export SMTP_PASSWORD=your-smtp-password
+export MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS='Fizzy <no-reply@example.com>'
+```
+
+Keep `RAILS_MASTER_KEY`, `SECRET_KEY_BASE`, registry credentials, and SMTP
+credentials private and use the same values for future deploys. If the SMTP server
+does not use authentication, leave `SMTP_USERNAME` and `SMTP_PASSWORD` set to
+empty strings. `SMTP_PORT` defaults to `587`, `SMTP_DOMAIN` defaults to
+`FIZZY_HOST`, `MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS` defaults to
+`Fizzy <no-reply@FIZZY_HOST>`, and `SMTP_ENABLE_STARTTLS_AUTO` defaults to
+`true`. Set `SMTP_AUTHENTICATION` as required by your provider (`plain`, `login`,
+or `cram_md5`), and set `SMTP_ENABLE_STARTTLS_AUTO=false` for a relay that does
+not support STARTTLS.
+
+The sample builder target is `amd64`. If your server uses a different
+architecture, update `builder.arch` in `config/deploy.yml` accordingly.
+
+## Install and deploy
+
+With the variables above set, run:
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal setup
+```
+
+Subsequent deploys use `bin/kamal deploy` with the same configuration and
+secrets. Keep the server's Docker volume named `fizzy-storage`; removing it
+permanently deletes the SQLite data and uploaded files. Back up this volume
+regularly, preferably while the application is stopped or using a consistent
+SQLite backup procedure.
+
+Solid Queue runs in the Puma process on this same server, so there is no separate
+jobs host or Redis service to provision.
